// ⚠ **EDITING THIS FILE MOVES A LINE NUMBER THE EXPECTATION PINS.** The report names the
// ASSERTION'S OWN line — `Expect`'s `file`/`line` default to `__file__`/`__line__`, which expand at
// the CALL SITE — so that number is part of the contract and not incidental. Insert a line above one
// and `expected.txt` is owed a regeneration; the gate's report will say which line differs.
// The JSON face reports the run the text face reports, so this fixture carries BOTH states: a
// report showing only one of them cannot show that the two are spelled differently (`passed` /
// `failed`), which is the parity `--json` exists to keep.
typealias Tally = int(i64.min to i64.max)

function halve(n Tally) returns Tally
	return n / 2
end 'halve'

test 'halving four gives two'
	try Expect.equal(halve(4), expected: 2)
end 'halving four gives two'

// Deliberately wrong — integer division truncates, so this is 2 and not 3.
test 'halving five gives three'
	try Expect.equal(halve(5), expected: 3)
end 'halving five gives three'
